# Widevine CDM persistent storage.
#
# The Level 3 CDM keeps its provisioned device identity under
# /data/vendor/mediadrm (the blob names /data/vendor/mediadrm/IDM directly) and
# creates the tree itself on first use. AOSP's
# android.hardware.drm@1.0-service.rc does not create it -- upstream leaves the
# directory to whichever vendor actually ships a plugin -- and hal_drm_default
# has no write access to the generic vendor_data_file label on /data/vendor, so
# without this the very first provisioning attempt fails and every DRM playback
# falls back to "no supported scheme".
#
# Create it here with the ownership Stock uses, so the HAL only ever needs
# permission *inside* the directory; sepolicy/drm gives it its own label.
on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/vendor/mediadrm 0770 media mediadrm
